    "scenario": "E1 for `atan`: substitution detection, NOT the correct-rounding proof (the eligibility probe carries that; [LEXP.3.9.2]). 32 of CORE-MATH's published hard-to-round arguments (src/binary64/atan/atan.wc at 6b84457310ad): the first 24 in file order that glibc 2.41's libm rounds differently from the correctly rounded value, then 8 it rounds the same, evenly spaced. `want` is MPFR's correctly rounded result (gmpy2, ieee(64)), not CORE-MATH's. One fact per argument; `r` fires iff the runtime's `atan` equals `want` to the last bit. PATH PINNED: the DS_FN_ATAN handler in runtime/src/libds/builtins.c calling ds_cm_atan, and ds.eval's transcendental arm calling ds.core_math.atan. Generated by scripts/gen_transcendental_e1.py; regenerate, do not edit.",
